  "notes": "{晴|は}らす means to actively clear away or dispel something negative — emotions, suspicion, or gloom. The object is always something undesirable.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {晴|は}れる (intransitive — to clear up, as in weather or mood)\n- Pattern: Xを{晴|は}らす\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{晴|は}らしている describes an ongoing effort to dispel something.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ストレスを{晴|は}らす (relieve stress)\n- {疑|うたが}いを{晴|は}らす (clear suspicion)\n- {鬱憤|うっぷん}を{晴|は}らす (vent frustration)\n- {恨|うら}みを{晴|は}らす (settle a grudge)\n- {汚名|おめい}を{晴|は}らす (clear one's name)\n\nUSAGE:\nImplies deliberate effort to remove something oppressive. Unlike {解消|かいしょう}する (to resolve/eliminate), {晴|は}らす has a more emotional, cathartic quality.",
